From: Project Luma <project-luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: complete in-flight requests on stop

With the software ISP a request completes only once its buffers are done
and the IPA has delivered its metadata. Frames still in flight when the
camera stops may never get that metadata: stopDevice() dropped their
frame info and left the requests queued, and Camera::stop() then hit the
queuedRequests_ assertion and aborted. Switching cameras in a GStreamer
application triggered it as soon as debayering took long enough for
frames to overlap the stop.

After cancelling the conversion queue, complete every request still
tracked in the frame info, cancelling any buffer that is still pending.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index 0095ea7..362db2e 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -211,6 +211,7 @@ public:
 	void clear();
 
 	SimpleFrameInfo *find(uint32_t frame);
+	std::vector<Request *> requests() const;
 
 private:
 	std::map<uint32_t, SimpleFrameInfo> frameInfo_;
@@ -233,6 +234,16 @@ void SimpleFrames::clear()
 	frameInfo_.clear();
 }
 
+std::vector<Request *> SimpleFrames::requests() const
+{
+	std::vector<Request *> requests;
+
+	for (const auto &[frame, info] : frameInfo_)
+		requests.push_back(info.request);
+
+	return requests;
+}
+
 SimpleFrameInfo *SimpleFrames::find(uint32_t frame)
 {
 	auto info = frameInfo_.find(frame);
@@ -1745,8 +1756,23 @@ void SimplePipelineHandler::stopDevice(Camera *camera)
 
 	video->bufferReady.disconnect(data, &SimpleCameraData::imageBufferReady);
 
-	data->frameInfo_.clear();
 	data->clearIncompleteRequests();
+
+	/*
+	 * Frames still in flight when the pipeline stops may never get their
+	 * metadata from the IPA. Complete their requests here, cancelling any
+	 * buffer still outstanding, or Camera::stop() finds them queued.
+	 */
+	for (Request *request : data->frameInfo_.requests()) {
+		if (request->status() != Request::RequestPending)
+			continue;
+		if (request->hasPendingBuffers())
+			cancelRequest(request);
+		else
+			completeRequest(request);
+	}
+
+	data->frameInfo_.clear();
 	data->conversionBuffers_.clear();
 
 	releasePipeline(data);
